          "file": "src/context/contentstackContext.tsx",
          "function": "ContentstackContext",
          "reason": "This is the central React context that holds all Contentstack page content (header, footer, page, etc.). Every component reads content via useContent → useContext(ContentstackContext). Live Preview must plug into this context — either by wrapping it with a LivePreviewProvider or by updating its value via onEntryChange when the CMS editor changes content. This is the primary attachment point for the new capability.",
          "fix": "Wrap the ContentstackContext with @contentstack/live-preview-utils integration: (1) Call LivePreview.init() at app startup (in _app.tsx or a dedicated provider component). (2) Create a new ContentstackLivePreviewProvider component that wraps ContentstackContext.Provider and subscribes to LivePreview.onEntryChange to update the context value when content changes in the CMS editor, causing all useContent consumers to re-render with preview data. The existing useContent hook and getValue utility require no changes — they already traverse the context object reactively.",
          "helper": "",
          "brokenLine": "export const ContentstackContext = createContext<IContentstackContext>({});",
          "fixVerified": null,
          "evidenceVerified": true,
          "prescriptionNote": "",
          "prescriptionUnderspecified": false
